// The Docker app (omarchy's lazydocker wrapper) runs `pkexec ... lazydocker` to
// reach the root-owned Docker socket, because the install user is deliberately
// not in the docker group. On this phone that pkexec can never be answered: the
// image locks the account password (image/configure.sh `passwd -l`), so the
// polkit dialog has no password to take and the on-screen keyboard will not
// raise for it, the TTY fallback is worse, and the Docker terminal blocks there
// with no way to cancel -- a soft-lock (fp4-defects.md D25). This is the same
// locked-password cause as the app store (49-moarchy-store.rules); only the
// surface differs.
//
// Grant just this action for wheel, so no prompt appears at all. It is no wider
// than a door already open: the same user holds `ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL` in
// /etc/sudoers.d/10-moarchy, and Docker-socket access is root-equivalent either
// way. Scoped to the lazydocker command so this is "let the Docker app
// through", not "authorize every pkexec".
//
// Not gated on subject.local && subject.active, for the same reason as
// 49-moarchy-store.rules: a shell restarted over ssh has no seat, and an
// active-only rule would put the unanswerable dialog back on a phone that
// cannot answer it.
//
// UNVERIFIED: lazydocker is not installed on the test handset, so the exact
// `command_line` string could not be confirmed. If the wrapper's command does
// not contain "lazydocker", this rule silently will not fire (the failure mode
// D26 hit). The broader alternative -- grant org.freedesktop.policykit.exec for
// wheel unconditionally -- fixes the whole class of terminal-pkexec soft-lock on
// this un-answerable device and is still bounded by the NOPASSWD sudo above; it
// is a security-posture call left to the owner.
polkit.addRule(function (action, subject) {
  if (action.id === "org.freedesktop.policykit.exec" &&
      subject.isInGroup("wheel")) {
    var cmd = action.lookup("command_line") || "";
    if (cmd.indexOf("lazydocker") !== -1) {
      return polkit.Result.YES;
    }
  }
});
